</div>

<div class="grammar-box">
  <span class="grammar-tag">📖 Grammar Focus — Negatives</span>
  <h4>Two words to learn: DON'T and DOESN'T</h4>
  <div class="formula">I / You / We / They + <em>don't</em> + verb<span>He / She / It + <em>doesn't</em> + verb (no -s on the main verb!)</span></div>
  <div class="grammar-grid">
    <div class="grammar-rule">
      <span class="rule-label">DON'T (I/You/We/They)</span>
      <div class="rule-text">
        I <em>don't</em> eat meat.<br>
        You <em>don't</em> like spiders.<br>
        We <em>don't</em> work on Sundays.<br>
        They <em>don't</em> speak French.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grammar-rule">
      <span class="rule-label">DOESN'T (He/She/It) ⚠️</span>
      <div class="rule-text">
        He <em>doesn't</em> eat meat. ✓<br>
        <s>He doesn't eats meat.</s> ✗<br><br>
        She <em>doesn't</em> like spiders. ✓<br>
        <s>She doesn't likes spiders.</s> ✗
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="grammar-rule" style="margin-top:10px;background:rgba(240,168,196,.2);border-color:rgba(240,168,196,.3);">
    <span class="rule-label" style="color:var(--pink);">⚠️ Critical Rule</span>
    <div class="rule-text">After DOESN'T, the main verb goes back to its BASE form (no -s).<br><em>She studies</em> → She <em>doesn't study</em> (NOT ~~doesn't studies~~)</div>
  </div>
</div>

