  <div class="grammar-grid">
    <div class="grammar-rule">
      <span class="rule-label">Adverbs of Frequency</span>
      <div class="rule-text">
        100% → <em>always</em> — I always drink water.<br>
        80% → <em>usually</em> — She usually works late.<br>
        60% → <em>often</em> — We often eat out.<br>
        40% → <em>sometimes</em> — He sometimes runs.<br>
        20% → <em>rarely / hardly ever</em><br>
        0% → <em>never</em> — They never watch TV.<br><br>
        ⚠️ Position: <em>BEFORE</em> the main verb.<br>
        I <em>always</em> eat breakfast. ✓<br>
        <s>I eat always breakfast.</s> ✗
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grammar-rule">
      <span class="rule-label">Time Expressions</span>
      <div class="rule-text">
        <em>every day / week / month / year</em><br>
        <em>on Mondays / on weekdays / on weekends</em><br>
        <em>in the morning / afternoon / evening</em><br>
        <em>at night / at 7am / at lunchtime</em><br>
        <em>once / twice / three times a week</em><br>
        <em>in the morning / at the weekend</em><br><br>
        ⚠️ Position: usually at the <em>END</em> of the sentence.<br>
        I go to the gym <em>on Mondays</em>. ✓
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

