    My name <input class="blank" id="fr1" data-answer="is" placeholder="be"> Valentina and I <input class="blank" id="fr2" data-answer="am" placeholder="be"> 32 years old. I <input class="blank" id="fr3" data-answer="live" placeholder="verb"> in Rosario with my husband and our two cats. I <input class="blank" id="fr4" data-answer="work" placeholder="verb"> as a primary school teacher — I love my job! My husband <input class="blank" id="fr5" data-answer="is" placeholder="be"> an architect. He <input class="blank" id="fr6" data-answer="doesn't work" placeholder="neg verb"> in an office — he <input class="blank" id="fr7" data-answer="works" placeholder="verb"> from home. There <input class="blank" id="fr8" data-answer="are" placeholder="is/are"> three rooms in our flat and there <input class="blank" id="fr9" data-answer="is" placeholder="is/are"> a lovely garden. We <input class="blank" id="fr10" data-answer="don't have" placeholder="neg verb"> a car. On weekends, we <input class="blank" id="fr11" data-answer="usually go" placeholder="frequency+verb"> for long walks or we <input class="blank" id="fr12" data-answer="cook" placeholder="verb"> together. I <input class="blank" id="fr13" data-answer="love" placeholder="verb"> cooking Italian food!
  </div>
  <div class="btn-row">
    <button class="btn btn-check" onclick="checkBlanks('fr',['is','am','live','work','is','doesn\'t work','works','are','is','don\'t have','usually go','cook','love'],13,this)">✓ Check All</button>
    <button class="btn btn-show" onclick="toggleAnswer('ans_fr')">Show Answers</button>
    <button class="btn btn-reset" onclick="resetBlanks2('fr',13)">↺ Reset</button>
  </div>
  <div class="answer-reveal" id="ans_fr"><span class="ar-label">Answers</span><li>is / am / live / work / is / doesn't work / works / are / is / don't have / usually go / cook / love</li></div>
  <div class="result-banner" id="res_fr"></div>
</div>

<div class="exercise">
  <div class="exercise-header"><div class="ex-num lila">37</div><div><div class="ex-type">Error Hunt</div><h4>Find and fix the mistakes. Each sentence has exactly ONE error.</h4></div></div>
  <div class="error-box">1. My brother <span class="err">don't speaks</span> English very well.</div>
  <input class="correction-input" placeholder="My brother..." id="eh1">
  <div class="error-box">2. She <span class="err">is work</span> in a hospital in the city centre.</div>
  <input class="correction-input" placeholder="She works..." id="eh2">
  <div class="error-box">3. There <span class="err">is</span> many restaurants in our neighbourhood.</div>
  <input class="correction-input" placeholder="There are..." id="eh3">
  <div class="error-box">4. I enjoy <span class="err">to swim</span> in the pool on Sundays.</div>
  <input class="correction-input" placeholder="I enjoy swimming..." id="eh4">
  <div class="error-box">5. We are always <span class="err">have</span> dinner together as a family.</div>
  <input class="correction-input" placeholder="We always have..." id="eh5">
  <div class="btn-row"><button class="btn btn-show" onclick="toggleAnswer('ans_eh')">Show Correct Versions</button></div>
  <div class="answer-reveal" id="ans_eh"><span class="ar-label">Corrected</span><li>My brother <strong>doesn't speak</strong> English very well. (doesn't + base verb, no -s)</li><li>She <strong>works</strong> in a hospital. (no "is" — not continuous tense)</li><li>There <strong>are</strong> many restaurants. (many = plural → there are)</li><li>I enjoy <strong>swimming</strong>. (enjoy + -ing, not infinitive)</li><li>We <strong>always have</strong> dinner. (no "are" — not continuous; frequency adverb before verb)</li></div>
